# Copy to .env in the project root and fill in the key for the provider you use.
# .env is gitignored — do not commit your real key.
#
# A .env file may ONLY set API keys. Everything else is ignored and reported in
# the review output. This is a security boundary: .env is searched in the working
# directory, which an agent may have pointed at a repository you just cloned, and
# a .env that could set `reviewer.command` would be arbitrary code execution
# inside the hook meant to prevent exactly that.
#
# Every other setting goes in the config file (see config.example.yaml) or the
# real environment. See the README for the full settings reference.
#
# Keys can also be kept out of files entirely: set `api_key_env` in the config to
# name whichever environment variable already holds your key.

# --- Pick one. With reviewer.provider "auto" (the default) the hook uses the
# --- first of these that is set, in this order. Leave all unset to run on local
# --- heuristics only.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Reminder: chatgpt and gemini also need `model` set in the config file. Only
# claude has a built-in default.
